     "when": "14 to 15 Nov",
     "tag": "UPDATED",
     "text": "The Federal Aviation Administration's (FAA) first review points to two sites: a radio site in El Dorado, Arkansas, where L3Harris was installing a new router, and a radar site in Amarillo, Texas. Blocking both calmed the network. The FAA has switched off a broadcasting feature on all the new routers. Officials still do not say whether it was human error or a faulty router. Flights were close to normal by Sunday.",
